Mavergreen's own, not yet upstream: llvm-install-name-tool (and llvm-objcopy on a linked image) handles
the load commands that name a dylib besides LC_LOAD_DYLIB and LC_LOAD_WEAK_DYLIB: LC_REEXPORT_DYLIB,
LC_LOAD_UPWARD_DYLIB and LC_LAZY_LOAD_DYLIB. llvm 22.1.8, and main as of 2026-11-24, refuse any image
carrying one, with "unsupported load command (cmd=0x8000001f)" for a re-export.

Why: the layout builder lists the commands it can carry over and refuses the rest, so as not to corrupt
what it does not understand; these three were left on a TODO. Each is a dylib_command, the same struct
and trailing name as LC_LOAD_DYLIB, which the reader and writer already carry as an opaque payload, so
there is nothing in them to lay out. libcxx22's libc++.1.dylib re-exports libc++abi.1.dylib, so
-id, -add_rpath and -change all failed on it (swift met it relinking libc++ for the @rpath migration).
-change now rewrites a matching re-exported, upward or lazy dylib's name too, as Apple's
install_name_tool does.

tests/install-name-reexport-test.sh is the regression test.

--- a/llvm/lib/ObjCopy/MachO/MachOLayoutBuilder.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/ObjCopy/MachO/MachOLayoutBuilder.cpp
@@ -431,6 +431,9 @@
     case MachO::LC_ID_DYLIB:
     case MachO::LC_LOAD_DYLIB:
     case MachO::LC_LOAD_WEAK_DYLIB:
+    case MachO::LC_REEXPORT_DYLIB:
+    case MachO::LC_LOAD_UPWARD_DYLIB:
+    case MachO::LC_LAZY_LOAD_DYLIB:
     case MachO::LC_UUID:
     case MachO::LC_SOURCE_VERSION:
     case MachO::LC_THREAD:
